    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="1122" n="1028" xml:id="pg1028"/>

                <head>No. 638.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. de Muruaga.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 15,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to say that I have
                    received letters from the Department of Justice and the Treasury assuring me
                    that their respective agents have been instructed to act in concert to prevent
                    any violation of the neutrality laws, by alleged forces gathering at Key West
                    and Tampa, hostile to the peace of Cuba.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
